      "id": "pell",
      "name": "Pell",
      "role": "tide-warden",
      "persona": "Pell counts the tide in reefmarks and trusts nothing she cannot measure. She is tired, blunt, and ashamed the Lantern has dimmed on her watch.",
      "knowledge": [
        "The Lantern Tower's vents are fed by glow-jelly oil, and the oil has thinned for a season.",
        "A shellward chime hung at the dock rings when the tide turns hard.",
        "The old lamp-wicks were pearls, set in the tower's crown by climbers."
      ],
      "secrets": [
        "Pell sold two crown pearls to Mira last winter to pay the warden crew."
      ],
